// Goat OS staging Grafana Alloy configuration.
//
// Deployed as the container config for the `goatos-stg-grafana-alloy` Cloud
// Run service (infra/envs/stg/observability.tf, asia-south1). Alloy's job
// here is narrow: terminate browser Real User Monitoring (RUM) telemetry from
// admin-web's `@grafana/faro-web-sdk` and forward it as OTLP to the OTel
// Collector, which then fans out to Cloud Trace / Cloud Logging / Google
// Managed Prometheus (GMP) exactly like every other signal in the stack. See
// docs/observability/OBSERVABILITY_DESIGN.md section 2.4.
//
// SIDECAR NOTE (see docs/observability/INFRA.md "Sidecar collector
// decision"): the collector used to be a standalone
// `goatos-stg-otel-collector` Cloud Run service that Alloy called over its
// public Cloud Run URL. That hop is public Alloy -> INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_ONLY
// collector, which cannot work without a Serverless VPC Access connector
// (none exists in this env) — so the collector now runs as a sidecar
// container in this SAME Cloud Run revision instead. GOATOS_OTEL_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT
// is `http://localhost:4318` (loopback, same revision, no TLS, no auth), set
// in infra/envs/stg/observability.tf.
//
// ASSUMPTION (flagged in docs/observability/INFRA.md): Alloy's faro.receiver
// forwards Faro payloads as OTel traces + logs only (Faro Web Vitals /
// "measurements" arrive as structured log records with numeric attributes,
// not as native OTel metrics). If true RUM *metrics* in GMP are required
// later, add an OTel Collector `transform`/`connector` stage that promotes
// selected measurement attributes to metrics — out of scope for this infra
// pass. Context7/live docs lookup was unavailable in this build session
// (auth error), so re-verify faro.receiver's exact argument/block names
// against the current Grafana Alloy reference before first deploy.

// Faro receiver: HTTP endpoint the browser SDK POSTs RUM payloads to.
// admin-web's faro-web-sdk `url` config point at this Cloud Run service's
// public HTTPS endpoint (Alloy runs INGRESS_TRAFFIC_ALL — see
// observability.tf — because browsers, not just internal GCP callers, must
// reach it).
//
// SECURITY: cors_allowed_origins is restricted to the real admin-web origin
// to prevent malicious websites from flooding the RUM sink with fake telemetry
// (which would consume quota and inflate billing). If the stg domain changes,
// update both this list and the admin-web SDK configuration. Rate limiting
// should be enforced at the Cloud Run service level (Cloud Armor policy) as a
// residual defense; this config-level CORS restriction is a first-line filter.
// See docs/observability/INFRA.md "Security" section.
faro.receiver "admin_web_rum" {
  server {
    listen_address       = "0.0.0.0"
    listen_port          = 12347
    cors_allowed_origins = ["https://stg.dashboard.mesha.sg"]
  }

  output {
    logs   = [otelcol.exporter.otlphttp.collector.input]
    traces = [otelcol.exporter.otlphttp.collector.input]
  }
}

// Forward everything Alloy receives to the sidecar OTel Collector in this
// same Cloud Run revision, over OTLP/HTTP on the loopback address (see the
// Cloud Run single-ingress-port note in otel-collector-config.yaml — the
// collector only exposes its OTLP/HTTP receiver on 4318, not OTLP/gRPC, so
// this MUST be `otelcol.exporter.otlphttp`, not `otelcol.exporter.otlp`
// (gRPC)). `insecure = true` because GOATOS_OTEL_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT is
// `http://localhost:4318` — plain loopback HTTP inside the same revision,
// never a network hop, so there is nothing to encrypt or authenticate.
otelcol.exporter.otlphttp "collector" {
  client {
    endpoint = sys.env("GOATOS_OTEL_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT")

    tls {
      insecure = true
    }
  }
}
